+		<English>[TAB]The Constitution established the judicial branch of the United States as a system distinct from the courts of the individual states. Congress organized the federal judiciary through the Judiciary Act of 1789, creating district and circuit courts beneath the Supreme Court.[PARAGRAPH:1]Federal courthouses serve as local seats of this national judicial system. As the United States expanded, Congress created and reorganized judicial districts and circuits to extend federal administration across new states and territories.[PARAGRAPH:1]Sources: https://www.uscourts.gov/about-federal-courts/court-role-and-structure; https://www.uscourts.gov/about-federal-courts/educational-resources/annual-observances/anniversary-federal-court-system</English>
